<main class="fb-container fb-main">
  <h1 class="fb-title fb-title--small">About Us</h1>

  <div class="fb-prose">
    <p>FieldBrik is an independent community and software project. We are a small team of builders with a stubborn attachment to the building games of 2006 to 2008, and to the idea that a platform should be a place people make things rather than a place things are sold to them.</p>

    <p>FieldBrik is free to use and built for members of all ages. The platform is under active development and is currently in public alpha testing. We value community feedback deeply, and we continue to make FieldBrik into a place that rewards curiosity in the young and the young at heart.</p>

    <p>FieldBrik 0.3 is a ground-up rebuild. The previous version had grown into something difficult to maintain: rules were implemented in several places, and a single change meant editing many files. This version puts every rule in one place, so moderation, permissions and accounts behave the same way everywhere.</p>

    <p>For more information about FieldBrik, visit the <a href="/news">News</a> and <a href="/help">Help</a> sections.</p>

    <p>FieldBrik is currently built by volunteers. If you would like to help with building, moderation or documentation, see the <a href="/support">Contact</a> page.</p>

    <p>Please contact us via email at <a href="/support">our support page</a>.</p>
  </div>
</main>

